Parent: 1478

## Context
Filed from git-erg (ticket 0306, PR MinhHaDuong/git-erg#386, raid 797d07), where the author made building
ID claims conditional on retiring more complicated or less reliable mechanisms. git-erg 0306 adds
`tickets/.claims/NNNN` (one line: slug and a random nonce): two branches that allocate the same ticket
number now get a git add/add conflict on merge or rebase, offline and on any forge, and `erg check` rejects
the ways that conflict can be silenced (`-X ours`, `merge=union`, a missing claim). Claims are on in a store
exactly when its `.claims/` directory exists, created by `erg migrate --claims`.

That covers both surfaces this repo's gate checks: the base tip (rebase/merge conflict) and a sibling open
PR (conflict at the second merge, before any duplicate lands; later than the CI job, which warned while
both were open).

## What retires here
- `scripts/check-cross-pr-ticket-collision.sh` (173 lines) and `tests/test_check_cross_pr_ticket_collision.sh`
  (450 lines): forge-dependent (gh auth, network, self-PR ambiguity, ticket 1325), switched off 2026-10-21
  with GitHub Actions.
- `.github/workflows/ticket-collision.yml`, the `scripts/local-ci.sh` wiring, the `CI.yml` comment and the
  `tickets/LOCAL.md` CI line.
- Any skill step that scans open PRs for a colliding ID (sweep `skills/` for `gh pr view` loops on ticket
  paths).

## Preconditions (do not start before)
- A git-erg release carries the claims (git-erg#386 merged and the bootstrap binary rebuilt), and this
  repo's `tickets/erg` is updated to it by `erg sync`.
- This store is migrated: `tickets/erg migrate --claims tickets/` committed, `tickets/.claims/` is not
  ignored (this repo ignores everything and allowlists paths: add `!tickets/.claims/` and
  `!tickets/.claims/*` to the allowlist; `erg migrate --claims` refuses an ignored claim path).

## Exit criteria
- [x] The preconditions hold.
- [x] The script, its test, the workflow, the local-ci wiring and the LOCAL.md line are removed.
- [x] A scratch test: two branches adding the same ticket number conflict on `tickets/.claims/NNNN`.
- [x] `make check` passes.

## Ripe (git-erg session, 2026-11-09 12:15Z)
Preconditions met. Pin moved twice by author decision 2026-11-09 (relayed by git-erg): take
sha256 `513cd3c4d916fd170d2d71b2cfe2182d4ab8db413822766db2e1ae5c5488b4ac`, revision bf71ab5
(git-erg bcbfa63), not 6a104262 (2d0dbea, ab519a3), dafb1d48 (8d24e74, aee15dd) nor 9ab13c9.
bf71ab5 behaves as 2d0dbea (only the revision stamp changed, git-erg docs/ renamed design/);
2d0dbea dropped the managed pre-commit rule that refused tickets/erg off the default branch. It adds required-claims checks, a pre-merge-commit hook, unclaimed-ticket
warnings and the 0309/0310 fixes. git-erg itself migrated in #393; the harness is the first
other adopter. That pin is also the one for the rollout to other repos.

Recipe, one PR: `tickets/erg sync --upstream`; check `tickets/erg version` prints that sha256;
`tickets/erg migrate --claims tickets`; `tickets/erg init` (shipped docs only);
`tickets/erg install --hooks` (core.hooksPath is the tracked `hooks/`: review how it chains with
the existing pre-commit hook and commit it in the same PR).

Expected fallout to fix in the same PR:
- Tests running the vendored binary on stores without `.claims/` go red: `tests/test_after_merge.py:508`
  (`erg check`), `tests/test_ticket_sweep.py` (close/archive); the new `erg new` refuses such
  stores. Give those test stores `.claims/` or run migrate on them; sweep tests/ for others.
- A few hundred advisory WARNs from the new "displaced log entry" lint: expected, unrelated.
- Any harness script that files a ticket in another repo with the harness's own binary is
  refused until that repo migrates; it must use the destination's `tickets/erg`.
- Old-binary tickets on other branches: after rebase, `tickets/erg migrate --claims tickets`
  only (refuses and lists a duplicate number: renumber by hand, rerun).
- Host: refresh `~/.local/bin/erg` on padme to the same sha256 after merge (author approved
  2026-11-09); note doudou for its own refresh.
